// @run
// @log 7
// @log 7
// @hint redundant type annotation: `a0` is inferred as `{v: i32}` — remove it to lean on inference
// @hint redundant type annotation: `b0` is inferred as `{v: i32}` — remove it to lean on inference
// THE TWO HINTS ARE DECLARED, NOT DESIGNED AWAY. `a0: A` and `b0: B` are the whole point of
// the program — they are what puts BOTH twin arms in a value position, and the checker
// calling each redundant (it infers the structural `{v: i32}` for both) is the same
// acceptance D280 quotes: the two names ARE one type to the checker while they were two
// `$fnsig`s to the emitter.
//
// THE FLOOR THIS FILE PINNED IS LIFTED, and the name is kept so the cross-references and
// the CHANGELOG entry that name it still resolve — the same graduation
// `arm-param-value-call-box-arg-floor.vl` beside it already made.
//
// It was the second witness that refuted a fix's first shape. D196 gives `paramTokOfTy` /
// `retTokOfTy` a nominal `variantRowOfTy` arm so a closure ANNOTATION naming a union arm
// keys the arm's `$fnsig` instead of its plain-struct layout twin's. Keyed RAW, that arm
// mints one `$fnsig` per variant ROW — `V0;>V0;` for `A` and `V1;>V1;` for `B` — while
// `buildVariantTwins` gives `A` and `B` ONE `uVarHeap` heap type, because their field sets
// match. TWO STRUCTURALLY IDENTICAL FUNCTYPES AT TWO INDICES OF ONE REC GROUP ARE DISTINCT
// TYPES IN WasmGC: the `call_indirect` type operand and the callee's declared functype
// disagreed, the module VALIDATED, and it trapped at run time with `indirect call type
// mismatch` after printing the first line. The shipped answer at the time was a DECLINE on
// a layout-twinned arm, which is the reject this file used to pin.
//
// D199 replaces the decline with the canonicalisation it was standing in for.
// `repVariantSlotRep` is the variant layer's `repStructSlotRep` — the smallest layout-twin
// row, computed from `repVariantSlotsTwin` so it is answerable at `$fnsig` INTERN time —
// and `repSigVariantTok` is the ONE place a `V<slot>;` digit is minted, so all five
// producers (`cloParamTok`, `cloRetKeySuffix`, `annParamKind`, `paramTokOfTy`,
// `retTokOfTy`) render the same row. Disassembled, both lambdas now declare ONE functype
// and both `call_indirect`s name it.
type A = { v: i32 }
type B = { v: i32 }
type U = A | B
const a0: A = { v: 7 }
const b0: B = { v: 7 }
function viaA(f: (A) => A, x: A) { print(f(x).v) }
function viaB(f: (B) => B, x: B) { print(f(x).v) }
viaA((p: A) => p, a0)
viaB((q: B) => q, b0)
